hadiths[65]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1455","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""You will find people like mines (of gold and silver). Those who were considered good and noble in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance are also good and noble in Islam, provided they acquire understanding of the religion. And you will find that the most suitable for leadership is the one who dislikes it the most. And the worst among people is the double-faced one, who comes to some people with one face and to others with another face."
"1456","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Muslims follow the Quraysh in leadership and caliphate, just as (the Arabs) in the time of disbelief also followed the Quraysh, and the condition of people is like that of mines. Those who were good and noble in the time of ignorance are also good and noble in the time of Islam, provided they acquire knowledge of the religion. You will find the best person to be the one who dislikes authority and leadership the most, until he is caught up in it."
"1457","When it reached Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this hadith that soon the king of the Arabs will be a Qahtani, Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry upon hearing this and stood up to deliver a sermon. First, he praised Allah as He deserves to be praised, then said: ""To proceed! It has reached me that some of you narrate such ahadith whose chain does not originate from the Book of Allah nor are they transmitted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So these people are ignorant; beware of them and their ideas, the very ideas that have led them astray. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This caliphate and leadership will remain among the Quraysh. Whoever opposes them, Allah will throw him down (overturn him), as long as (the Quraysh) uphold the religion and the Shari'ah."
"1458","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of Quraysh, Ansar, Juhaina, Muzaina, Aslam, Ashja‘, and Ghifar—all these tribes are my well-wishers, and apart from Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him), they have no protector."
"1459","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""This caliphate will remain among the Quraysh as long as there are two men of them left (in the world)."
"1460","Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I and Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and submitted: You have given (the share of near relatives) to Banu Muttalib, while we (Banu Umayyah) and Banu Muttalib have the same relationship with you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “That is true, but Banu Hashim and Banu Muttalib have always been together as one.”"
"1461","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever knowingly claims someone other than his father as his father, he has committed disbelief. Whoever claims to belong to a people to whom he does not belong, let him take his place in the Hellfire."
"1462","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The greatest slander (and most severe lie) is that a man claims someone other than his father as his father, or says he saw in a dream what his eyes did not see, or attributes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something which he did not say.”"
"1463","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while standing on the pulpit: ""Allah has forgiven the tribe of Ghifar, and Allah has saved the tribe of Aslam, and the tribe of 'Usayyah has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"1464","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Aqra’ bin Habis (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that those people have pledged allegiance to you who used to steal the belongings of the pilgrims, meaning the people of the tribes of Aslam, Ghifar, and Muzaynah, and I think he also said, ""and the people of Juhaynah""—this doubt is from Ibn Abi Ya’qub, the narrator. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell me! Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Juhaynah (these four tribes) are better than Banu Tamim, Banu Amir, Asad, and Ghatafan. Are the former (four) ruined and destroyed?"" Aqra’ said, ""Yes!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they are better than them."
"1465","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tribe of Aslam and Ghifar and some people from Muzaina and Juhaina—or he said: some people from Juhaina or Muzaina—will be better in the sight of Allah, or he said: on the Day of Resurrection, than Asad, Tamim, Hawazin, and Ghatafan."
"1466","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until a man from Qahtan becomes king and drives the people with his staff."
"1467","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): We fought in jihad with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time many of the Muhajirun had gathered around him. Among these Muhajirun was a man who was very playful; he struck an Ansari on his buttocks. The Ansari became very angry and called out to his people, saying, ""O Ansar! Come quickly (listen to my plea)!"" The Muhajir said, ""O Muhajirun! Come quickly!"" Hearing this commotion, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of his tent and said, ""What is this call of the days of ignorance?"" Then he asked, ""What is the matter?"" The people said, ""A Muhajir struck an Ansari on his buttocks."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Leave these filthy matters of ignorance."" And Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul (the hypocrite) said, ""The Muhajirun are calling their people against us, so when we reach Madinah, surely the honorable will expel the lowly from it."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should I not strike the neck of this filthy man?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""No! People will say that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kills his own companions."
"1468","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Amr bin Luhayy bin Qam'ah bin Khindaf was the father of the Khuza'ah (the tribe of Khuza'ah)."
"1469","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): He said that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw ‘Amr bin ‘Amir bin Luhayy al-Khuza‘i dragging his intestines in Hell; he was the first to introduce the custom of Sa’ibah."
"1470","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was a man from the tribe of Ghifar. We received news that a man had appeared in Makkah who claimed to be a Prophet. So I said to my brother, “Go to this man, speak to him, and tell me about his situation.” He went, met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and then returned. I asked him, “What did you see?” He said, “By Allah, I saw a man who commands good and forbids evil.” (He only said this much.) I said to him, “This report does not satisfy me.” So I took a water-skin and my staff and set out for Makkah. I did not know the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not think it appropriate to ask anyone about him. I kept drinking Zamzam water and stayed in the mosque. Then (one day) Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by me and said, “You seem to be a traveler.” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I replied, “Yes!” He (Ali) said, “Come with me to my house.” I went with him; he did not ask me anything, nor did I tell him anything. The next morning, I went to the mosque again, hoping to ask someone about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I found no one who could tell me anything about him. (Abu Dharr said:) Then Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by me again and said, “Has this man (meaning me) not found his place yet?” I said, “No.” He said, “Come with me.” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me, “Tell me, what is your purpose? For what reason have you come to this city?” I said to him, “If you promise to keep it secret, I will tell you.” He said, “I will do so.” So I said, “We received news that a man has appeared here who claims to be a Prophet. I sent my brother to speak to him, but the report he brought did not satisfy me, so I decided to meet him myself.” (Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Indeed, you have found the right path (by meeting me). I also go to him, so follow me. Wherever I enter, you also enter. If I see anything that causes fear on the way, I will stand by a wall as if I am cleaning my shoe, and you should pass by.” Then (Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) set off, and I (Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him) went with him until he entered a house, and I entered with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was there. I said to him, “Teach me Islam.” So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me, and I became Muslim right there (at that moment). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: “O Abu Dharr! Conceal this matter (your faith) and return to your homeland. When you hear of our victory, then come.” I said, “(O Messenger of Allah!) By Him Who sent you with the truth, I will proclaim this (testimony) among them (the disbelievers), whatever may happen.” So (Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him) went to the mosque, where the disbelievers of Quraysh were present. (Abu Dharr) said, “O people of Quraysh! I bear witness that there is no (true) god except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His servant and His Messenger.” (Upon hearing this) they said, “Get up and deal with this apostate!” So they stood up and beat me severely, intending to kill me. Abbas ibn Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) saw me, leaned over me, and then turned to them and said, “Woe to you! (What are you doing?) You are killing a man from the tribe of Ghifar, while your trade and travel route passes by their territory.” (Upon hearing this) they left me alone. The next day, I came to the mosque again and proclaimed as I had done the previous day. (The disbelievers of Quraysh) said, “Get up! Deal with this apostate!” and they beat me as they had done the day before. Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) saw me again, came and leaned over me, and said the same thing he had said the previous day. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: This is how Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) embraced Islam."
"1471","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): When this verse was revealed: ""O Prophet! Warn your near relatives (of Allah's punishment),"" the Prophet (peace be upon him) began to call out: ""O people of Banu Fihr! O people of Banu Adi!"" These were all clans of the Quraysh."
"1472","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Hazrat Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) to satirize the polytheists of Mecca. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am also from their family."" So Hazrat Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""With the excellence of my poetry, I will separate you from those polytheists just as a hair is taken out from flour."
"1473","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I have five names: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and Maahi (i.e., the one who erases—Allah will erase disbelief through me), and Haashir (i.e., people will be gathered after me), and ‘Aaqib (i.e., the Seal of the Prophets—there will be no new prophet after me in the world).”"
"1474","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Are you not amazed at how Allah turns away the insults and curses of Quraysh from me? They insult and curse 'Mudhammam', and they curse 'Mudhammam', while I am Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"1475","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My example and the example of the other prophets is like that of a person who built a house and made it complete and beautiful, except for the place of one brick. People began to go around the house and were amazed, saying: 'If only this brick were placed, how excellent and complete this house would be.'"
"1476","In another narration from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), it is transmitted in addition that .... but in one corner, a space equal to one brick was left. And at the end, he said: ""I am that brick, and I am the Seal of the Prophets."
"1477","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): ""At the time of his death, the age of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sixty-three years."
"1478","Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that at that time his age was ninety-four (94) years, but he was still quite strong, and I know that my senses, ears, and eyes all still function—this is the blessing of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). My maternal aunt took me to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, this is my nephew, he is ill, please supplicate for him."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated for me."
"1479","Narrated Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) led the Asr prayer, then went on foot (on the way) and saw Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him), who was playing with the children. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) lifted him onto his shoulder and said, ""May my father be sacrificed for you, you resemble the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and do not resemble Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."" Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was laughing upon hearing this."
"1480","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he (peace be upon him) resembled Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). So it was said to him (Abu Juhaifah), ""Describe the appearance of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" He said: He (peace be upon him) was fair-skinned, his hair was partly white and partly black, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to be given thirteen camels, but we had not yet taken those camels when he (the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"1481","It was said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, who was a companion of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), ""Did you see the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) when he was old?"" He replied, ""There were some white hairs between his lower lip and his chin."
"1482","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was of medium stature, neither very tall nor very short. His complexion was fair with a reddish tinge, not completely white (like lime), nor very wheatish (yellowish), but rather reddish-white. His hair was neither very curly nor completely straight. Revelation descended upon him at the age of forty. He (peace be upon him) stayed in Makkah for ten years. Revelation (the Qur'an) continued to descend, and he stayed in Madinah for ten years. At the time of his passing, there were not even twenty white hairs in his blessed head and beard. (Note: The Arabs sometimes count in tens and leave out the units, although the Prophet (peace be upon him) stayed in Makkah for thirteen years after prophethood.)"
"1483","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in another narration says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither very tall nor short, neither completely white in complexion nor completely wheatish yellow, neither had very curly hair nor completely straight hair. Allah Almighty bestowed Prophethood (revelation of the Qur'an) upon him at the end of his fortieth year of blessed age... and the rest of the hadith is narrated (see the previous hadith:)."
"1484","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most handsome, pleasant-faced, beautiful, and the best in character among all people. In stature, he was neither very tall nor very short."
"1485","It was asked from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apply dye?"" He said: ""No, only a little whiteness had appeared on both his temples."
"1486","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of medium height and there was a gap between his shoulders (his chest was broad). His hair reached his earlobes. I saw him wearing a red (striped) mantle, and I have never seen anyone more beautiful than him."
"1487","It is narrated in another narration from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked, “Was the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a sword (long and thin)?” He replied, “No, rather it was round and radiant like the moon.”"
"1488","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing prayer (at noon) in the valley of Batha, and in front of him a spear (as a sutrah) was fixed.... This hadith has already passed (see the Book: Description of Prayer... Chapter: The Sutrah of the Imam is also the Sutrah of the Followers) and in this narration, Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that people stood up and began to take the hand of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wipe it over their faces (for blessings). Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I also took the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it on my face, and it was cooler than ice and more fragrant than musk."
"1489","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have continued to be among the best generations of people (that is, among noble and pure lineages) from (the time of) Adam (peace be upon him) until the generation in which I was born."
"1490","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that in the beginning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would let the hair of his forelock hang forward, while the polytheists would part their hair. The People of the Book would let their hair hang, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), in matters where no command had come, preferred to agree with the People of the Book rather than the polytheists. Then after that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began to part his hair."
"1491","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither foul-mouthed nor did he use bad language, and he used to say: “The best among you are those who have the best character.”"
"1492","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was given a choice between two matters, he would choose the easier of the two, as long as it was not sinful. If it was sinful, he would keep away from it more than anyone else. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never took revenge for his own sake, but when the limits of Allah were transgressed, he would take revenge for the sake of Allah."
"1493","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have not seen silk or any (other) fine cloth softer than the palm of Allah’s Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor have I smelled any fragrance better than the fragrance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1494","Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was more modest than a veiled virgin girl."
"1495","In one narration it is stated (Shu’bah, may Allah have mercy on him, says) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked something, it could be known from his face."
"1496","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never criticized any food. If he desired it, he would eat it; if he disliked it, he would leave it (without criticizing it)."
"1497","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to speak in such a manner (calmly and with pauses) that if someone wanted to count (the words), they could count them."
"1498","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not speak hastily in the manner that you do."
"1499","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him)` narrates the incident of that night (the Night of Ascension), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was taken from Masjid al-Ka'bah, that before revelation descended upon him, three angels came to him while he (peace and blessings be upon him) was sleeping in Masjid al-Haram (between Sayyiduna Ja'far bin Abi Talib and Sayyiduna Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with them). One of them (the angels) said, ""Who among them is he (who has been commanded to be taken)?"" The second said, ""He (the one in the middle) is the best among them."" The third said, ""Take the one who is the best among all of them."" That night, only this happened, and after that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw them on another night, just as he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to see with his heart, and the eyes of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would sleep but his heart would not sleep, and this is the state of all the Prophets: their eyes sleep but their hearts do not sleep. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) took the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with him and ascended to the heavens."
"1500","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the place of Zawraa when a vessel of water was brought to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in that vessel, then water began to gush forth from his fingers, and all the people performed ablution. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, ""How many people were you?"" He replied, ""Three hundred or close to three hundred."
"1501","Narrated Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him): We used to consider miracles as blessings and favors from Allah, while you are afraid of them. We were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the water became scarce. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If anyone has any leftover water, bring it."" So people brought a vessel in which there was a little water. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his hand in that vessel and then said: ""Come, take the blessed water, and the blessing is from Allah."" (Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him) says: I myself saw that water was gushing from the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time, while eating, we used to hear the food glorifying Allah."
"1502","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until you fight with people who wear hairy shoes.... This lengthy hadith has already passed (see the Book: On Jihad and Military Expeditions... Chapter: The Mention of Fighting with the Turks), and at the end of this narration he says that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: '... And a time will come when any one of you will prefer to see me more than having all his family, wealth, and property.'"
"1503","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until you fight the people of Khuz and Kirman (Persians), whose faces will be red, noses flat, and eyes small. Their faces will be like layered shields, and they will wear shoes made of hair."
"1504","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""This tribe of Quraysh (Banu Umayyah) will destroy the people."" The Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: ""Then what do you command us to do?"" He said: ""I wish people would keep away from them."
"1505","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard (from the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him), who was truthful and was made truthful, saying: ""The destruction of my Ummah will be at the hands of a few young men from the Quraysh."" So Marwan said, ""A few young men?"" (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah said:) ""If you wish, I can also mention their names: so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, and so-and-so, the son of so-and-so."
"1506","`Sayyiduna Hudhayfah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good things, and I used to ask him about evils (which would occur after him) out of fear that I might fall into them. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this goodness through you. Will there be evil after this goodness?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Yes."" I said, ""Will there be goodness after that evil?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Yes, but there will be smoke in it."" I asked, ""What is smoke?"" He said, ""There will be people who will not follow my way; some of their deeds will be good and some bad."" I said, ""Will there be evil after that goodness?"" He said, ""Yes! There will be people who will stand at the gates of Hell, calling towards it; whoever responds to their call, they will throw him into Hell."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said, ""They will be from our people (Muslims) outwardly, and will speak our language."" I said, ""If I live to see that time, what do you command me to do?"" He said, ""Stay with the group of Muslims and their rightful leader."" I said, ""What if there is no group or leader at that time?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Then keep away from all those sects, even if you have to chew the root of a tree (due to hunger) until death overtakes you; this will be better for you than joining them."
"1507","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When I narrate to you any hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then understand that for me, falling from the sky to the earth is easier than attributing a lie to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And when I tell you things that happened between me and you, then (there is no harm in it because) fighting is the name of strategy and deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""In the last era, some people will be born who will have small teeth, little intellect, and will be foolish."" They will say things that are better than all the sayings of the world, but they will leave the religion of Islam just as an arrow leaves the bow (nothing of it remains attached). Faith will not go below their throats. Wherever you find these people, kill them. Whoever kills them will receive the reward for that killing on the Day of Resurrection."
"1508","Sayyiduna Khabbab bin Al-Aratt (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the persecution of the disbelievers. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was reclining on his cloak in the shade of the Ka'bah. We said, ""Why do you not seek (Allah's) help for us? Why do you not pray for us?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among those before you, there were people for whom a pit would be dug in the ground, then they would be placed in it, and a saw would be brought and placed on their heads and they would be cut into two pieces, but even then they would not turn away from their true religion. And iron combs would be run over their bones and flesh, but even then they would not abandon their faith. By Allah, Allah will surely complete this religion, until a rider will travel from Sana'a to Hadramaut fearing none but Allah, or only fearing the wolf lest it should eat his sheep, but you are being impatient."
"1509","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found Sayyiduna Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) missing (he was not present). A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I will bring you news of him."" He went and saw that Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting in his house with his head bowed (in grief). He asked, ""What is the matter?"" Thabit said, ""It is bad; I used to raise my voice above the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so all my deeds have been wasted and I am among the people of Hell."" That man returned and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he says such and such. (The narrator Musa bin Anas) says that then that man went again (to Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him) with this great good news that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Go to him (Thabit) and say that you are not among the people of Hell, but rather among the people of Paradise."
"1510","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man recited Surah Al-Kahf, and there was a horse tied in his house which began to get restless. So he ended his prayer (because he was reciting during prayer) and saw that there was a cloud that had covered the whole house. He mentioned this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) said: “O so-and-so! Continue reciting the Qur’an. This is tranquility which descended because of the recitation of the Qur’an.”"
"1511","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to visit a Bedouin who was ill, and it was the blessed habit of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he went to visit a sick person, he would say: ""No worry, InshaAllah this illness will purify you from sins."" So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same to him: ""No worry, InshaAllah this illness will purify you from sins."" He said, ""You (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say there is no worry, but no, it is not so at all. Here the situation is that the fever is raging or overpowering an old man, and it will not leave him without taking him to the grave."" So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Alright, then it will be so."
"1512","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a man was a Christian, then he became a Muslim and learned Surah Al-Baqarah and Al-Imran, and he used to write (revelation) for the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). Then he became a Christian again and said, ""What does Muhammad (peace be upon him) know except what I write for him?"" Then Allah caused him to die, so the people buried him, but in the morning his body was lying on the ground. The (Christian) people said, ""This is the work of Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his companions. When he left them and ran away, they came at night, dug up the grave, and threw our companion's body out."" So they dug a very deep grave and buried him again. In the morning, they saw that the earth had thrown his body out again. They said, ""This is the work of Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his companions. They dug up our companion's grave and threw him out because he left them and ran away."" Then (for the third time) they dug an even deeper grave, as deep as they could, and buried him, but in the morning they saw again that the earth had thrown his body out. When they became certain that this was not the work of any human (but rather the wrath of Allah), they threw his body (in the open field) or left it as it was."
"1513","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do you have carpets?"" I said, (we are poor people) how would we have carpets? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""But soon you will have (fine) carpets."" Now, when I say to my wife, ""Come, remove our carpet from here,"" she says, ""Did not the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Soon you will have carpets'?"" So I remain silent."
"1514","´Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I said to Umayyah bin Khalaf that I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that they will kill you. Umayyah said, “Me?” Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Yes.” Umayyah said, “By Allah! Muhammad’s (peace be upon him) word is never false.” So Allah Almighty had him killed on the day of Badr. There is also an incident in this hadith, but the main content of the hadith is this."
"1515","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) while Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) was present with him. He (Jibreel) began talking with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then got up (and left). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), ""(Do you know) who that was?"" (or asked a similar question). She replied, ""That was Dihyah Kalbi"" (who was a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him). Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""By Allah! I thought it was Dihyah until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed the people and referred to Jibreel (peace be upon him), and in the sermon he narrated those things which Jibreel (peace be upon him) had said to him."
"1516","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw (in a dream) that people were gathered in a field. Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and drew one or two buckets of water from a well, but with some weakness. May Allah forgive him. Then Umar (bin Khattab) took hold of the bucket, and as soon as it came into his hands, it became a large bucket. I have not seen such a strong champion doing work like him. He drew so much water that people watered their camels and took them to their resting places."
"1517","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that a man and a woman among them had committed adultery. (They asked:) ""What do you command?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What do you find written about stoning in the Torah?"" They said: ""We disgrace the adulterer and adulteress (by blackening their faces and humiliating them) and flog them."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You are lying. The command of stoning is in the Torah."" They brought the Torah, opened it, and a Jew placed his hand over the verse of stoning and began to read what was before and after it. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""Lift your hand."" He lifted his hand, and there was the verse of stoning. (The Jews) said: ""O Muhammad! He has spoken the truth; indeed, the command of stoning is in the Torah."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and both of them (the adulterer and the adulteress) were stoned."
"1518","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the moon split into two pieces during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(O people!) Bear witness.”’"
"1519","Narrated from Sayyiduna Urwah Al-Bariqi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a dinar and told him to buy a goat. He went and bought two goats for one dinar, then sold one of them for one dinar, and brought one goat and one dinar to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for blessings in his trade (and due to the blessing of the Prophet’s prayer, Urwah’s condition became such) that if he bought dust, he would also profit from it."
